# Kilnmark's settings for compose.yaml. Copy this file to .env beside compose.yaml, fill in every
# required value, and keep .env readable only by the people who run Kilnmark:
#   cp .env.example .env && chmod 600 .env
# compose.yaml has no default password or token: it refuses to start while a required value is
# missing or empty, and names it.

# Required. Password of Kilnmark's database; the kilnmark user owns it and is its PostgreSQL
# superuser. Use a long random value, for example the output of: openssl rand -base64 32
# It takes effect when the database volume is first created; changing it later also needs
# ALTER USER kilnmark PASSWORD '...' in the database.
KILNMARK_DB_PASSWORD=

# Required. Kilnmark's admin API token: km_ followed by 43 or more letters, digits, - or _.
# Make one with: echo km_$(openssl rand -base64 32 | tr '+/' '-_' | tr -d '=')
# Sign in with it, then create personal tokens under API tokens. Changing it sets the old one aside.
KILNMARK_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# Required. The deployment mode (ADR 0051): production, or starter-pack for training and development
# only, with the Starter Pack's example data and people. The control script writes it at install
# (starter-pack with --starter) and Kilnmark records it at the first start: changing it here never
# moves an install from one mode to the other (Kilnmark refuses to start), and a Starter Pack install
# never becomes a production one: install afresh. Lower case, exactly one of the two. A Starter
# Pack install always signs in with the bundled Keycloak (COMPOSE_PROFILES=auth and the Keycloak
# settings below, which install writes); Kilnmark does not start without it.
KILNMARK_MODE=

# Starter Pack installs only. Password of kilnmark_samples, the Starter Pack's own login to its own
# database on Kilnmark's PostgreSQL server (ADR 0051). The control script makes one on install, up
# and upgrade of a Starter Pack install; by hand, a long random value (16 characters or more).
# KILNMARK_SAMPLES_DB_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Your own folder, as a full path on this machine, for file sources to read: Kilnmark
# sees it read-only at /srv/share (it writes only in its own folder, /srv/files). Kilnmark's user
# (uid 1001 in the container) must be able to read it. Unset: /srv/share is empty.
# KILNMARK_FILES_DIR=/srv/kilnmark-files

# Optional, with the bundled Keycloak. How long a temporary password from the people commands may
# wait unused before its person is disabled (people activate gives a new one): 1 to 720 hours.
# Checked at every start and every hour (people expire, which up sets up), so at most an hour late.
# KILNMARK_PEOPLE_ACTIVATION_HOURS=72

# Starter Pack installs only. allowed: the Starter Pack's five example people may be made in the
# bundled Keycloak (the auth profile, below) with: kilnmark.sh starter people (Windows: kilnmark.cmd
# starter people), which asks you for their password and never shows it. keycloak-setup makes them,
# with Keycloak's own admin; Kilnmark holds no Keycloak credential. Remove this line and run up to
# delete them again.
# KILNMARK_STARTER=allowed

# Optional. The ports Kilnmark and its database are published on (the database on this machine only).
# KILNMARK_PORT=8780
# KILNMARK_DB_PORT=5442

# Optional. Sign-in with your organisation's identity provider over OpenID Connect (Entra ID, Okta,
# Ping, ADFS, Keycloak, ...), beside API tokens; INSTALL.md, "Sign in with your identity provider".
# Register Kilnmark with the provider as a web application whose redirect URI is
# https://<kilnmark's address>/api/v1/auth/login, then set:
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ENABLED=true
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ISSUER=https://login.example.com/your-tenant/v2.0
# KILNMARK_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# KILNMARK_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# (Until they are set, Docker Compose notes that KILNMARK_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET and the Keycloak
# values below are not set; that is all.)
# KILNMARK_OIDC_PROVIDER_NAME=Example SSO
# Groups (as the provider's groups claim names them, comma-separated) and the role each gives:
# KILNMARK_OIDC_VIEWER_GROUPS=
# KILNMARK_OIDC_STEWARD_GROUPS=
# KILNMARK_OIDC_DESIGNER_GROUPS=
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ADMIN_GROUPS=
# Designers in these groups see values of columns marked sensitive:
# KILNMARK_OIDC_UNMASK_GROUPS=
# A sign-in renews itself with the provider's refresh token. Entra ID and Okta issue one only when
# asked for offline_access (never set it for Keycloak):
# KILNMARK_OIDC_SCOPES=offline_access
# Kilnmark must be on HTTPS for this; behind a proxy that ends TLS, also:
# KILNMARK_OIDC_BEHIND_TLS_PROXY=true

# Optional on a production install, required on a Starter Pack install. Keycloak, bundled for an
# organisation with no identity provider of its own (add people with kilnmark.sh people add, people
# import or Keycloak's console; backup includes its database); started
# with: podman compose --profile auth up -d (INSTALL.md, "Keycloak, if you have no identity
# provider"). To start and stop it with Kilnmark on every plain podman compose up -d and down, set:
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=auth
# Each secret is a long random value, for example: openssl rand -base64 32
# KILNMARK_KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD=
# KILNMARK_KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# Keycloak's first admin is made on its first start only: changing these later changes nothing
# (change the password in Keycloak's console, then here).
# KILNMARK_KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin
# Keycloak is published on this machine only, on this port; other machines reach it through a proxy
# that ends TLS. Where browsers reach Keycloak and Kilnmark (behind a proxy, their https://
# addresses); the Keycloak address follows the port:
# KILNMARK_KEYCLOAK_PORT=8180
# KILNMARK_KEYCLOAK_URL=http://localhost:8180
# KILNMARK_URL=http://localhost:8780
# Then sign-in with it, using the realm keycloak-setup makes:
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ENABLED=true
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ISSUER=http://keycloak:8080/realms/kilnmark
# KILNMARK_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=kilnmark
# KILNMARK_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# KILNMARK_OIDC_PROVIDER_NAME=Keycloak
# KILNMARK_OIDC_VIEWER_GROUPS=kilnmark-viewers
# KILNMARK_OIDC_STEWARD_GROUPS=kilnmark-stewards
# KILNMARK_OIDC_DESIGNER_GROUPS=kilnmark-designers
# KILNMARK_OIDC_ADMIN_GROUPS=kilnmark-admins
# KILNMARK_OIDC_UNMASK_GROUPS=kilnmark-sensitive-data
# For a demonstration, the Starter Pack's example people: KILNMARK_STARTER, above.

# Optional. The longest an API token may last, for example 90d: new tokens must expire within it,
# and older ones stop working (check Settings, Access review before setting it). Unset: no limit.
# KILNMARK_TOKEN_MAX_LIFETIME=90d

# Optional. true: a designer token asked to see sensitive values waits until a second person
# approves it under API tokens, so no one person can give that access alone. Needs sign-in with your
# identity provider (above): the two people are told apart by it.
# KILNMARK_UNMASK_APPROVAL=true

# Optional. Host names bulk import rewrites when asked to (remapHosts=true), as from=to pairs.
# KILNMARK_SOURCES_HOST_MAP=localhost=host.docker.internal

# Not set here: the key that encrypts stored source passwords is generated on first start in the
# keys volume (/var/lib/kilnmark/secret.key). Back that volume up apart from the database.
